   845	/// `PatrolSpawner` (PatrolSpawner.java:16-91): the world-tick spawner that seeds illager
   846	/// patrols away from villages, one of which carries the ominous banner as its captain.
   847	///
   848	/// Ported field for field: the `12000 + nextInt(1200)` reschedule (line 26), the daylight gate
   849	/// (line 27), the 1-in-5 chance (line 28), the random non-spectator player (lines 29-32), the
   850	/// "not within 2 sections of a village" refusal (line 33), the `(24 + nextInt(24))` signed
   851	/// offset on each horizontal axis (lines 34-36), the loaded-chunk requirement (line 38), the
   852	/// `ceil(effectiveDifficulty) + 1` group size (line 40), leader-first with break-on-failure
   853	/// (lines 44-47) and the `nextInt(5) - nextInt(5)` per-member walk (lines 52-53).
   854	///
   855	/// Scope reductions, each because the vanilla dependency has no analogue in Pumpkin:
   856	/// - `EnvironmentAttributes.CAN_PILLAGER_PATROL_SPAWN` (line 39) - no environment-attribute
   857	///   system exists; the biome/dimension gate is therefore not applied.
   858	/// - The Y lookup uses `World::get_top_block` (the `WORLD_SURFACE` heightmap) rather than
   859	///   `Heightmap.Types.MOTION_BLOCKING_NO_LEAVES` (line 43); Pumpkin tracks the latter on chunks
   860	///   but exposes no world-level accessor for it.
   861	/// - `PatrollingMonster.setPatrolLeader`/`findPatrolTarget`/`setPatrolling`
   862	///   (PatrollingMonster.java:102-131) and `LongDistancePatrolGoal` are not ported - Pumpkin's
   863	///   `PillagerEntity` carries no patrol-target state, so spawned patrols use the pillager's
   864	///   ordinary wander and target goals instead of marching toward a distant target. The captain
   865	///   is still marked the way vanilla marks it, by the head-slot banner
   866	///   (PatrollingMonster.java:76).
   867	/// - Killing a captain does not yield an ominous bottle. Vanilla routes that through the
   868	///   `minecraft:pillager` entity loot table's `type_specific/raider {is_captain: true}`
   869	///   predicate; `pumpkin_util::loot_table::LootCondition::EntityProperties` models only
   870	///   `expected_type`/`is_on_fire`/`mainhand_enchantment_tag`, so the predicate cannot be
   871	///   expressed. Drinking an ominous bottle already triggers the whole raid chain
   872	///   (`LivingEntity::apply_effect_tick`), so this is the one missing link in the
   873	///   captain-to-raid loop.
   874	#[derive(Default)]
   875	pub struct PatrolSpawner {
   876	    next_tick: i32,
   877	}
